      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The best time to replace a roof in Utah is late spring (May to early June) or early fall (September to October).",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "late spring (May to early June) or early fall (September to October)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Why These Windows Work Best"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Mild Temperatures: Asphalt shingles need temperatures roughly between 40\u00b0F and 85\u00b0F to flex properly without cracking and to let the factory-applied sealant strips activate and bond."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Predictable Weather: These months avoid the extreme, damaging heat of mid-summer and the freezing snow or ice dams of mid-winter."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Winter Prep: Replacing your roof in early fall ensures your home is fully sealed and ready before heavy mountain and valley snowstorms arrive."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Season-by-Season Breakdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Spring (April\u2013May): Great for sealing as temperatures warm up, but contractors book up fast after winter."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Summer (June\u2013August): Highly productive with long daylight hours, but extreme mid-summer heat can make shingles overly soft and prone to scuffing from workers' boots."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fall (September\u2013October): Considered the gold standard for crisp air and perfect curing temperatures, though it is a peak busy season for local contractors."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Winter (November\u2013March): Challenging and generally avoided unless it is an emergency. Cold shingles become brittle, and sealant strips will not activate until warmer weather returns, requiring hand-sealing."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, I can share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The signs that indicate your roof needs immediate replacement rather than waiting for an ideal seasonTips on how to choose a reputable local roofing contractor in Utah"
      },
